faqTitleEm: staging before selling?
faqs:
- q: What is home staging?
  a: Home staging means preparing a home so it shows well to buyers. At Chayce it sits alongside sorting and declutter help, because a home with fewer belongings is easier to stage and to move.
- q: Is staging included in your packages?
  a: Staging for sale is included from Silver Comfort at {silver}. Gold Prestige at {gold} adds full home staging with photography, estate agent and solicitor liaison, viewings and up to six weeks of storage. Bronze Essentials does not include staging.
- q: When should staging start?
  a: Before the property is listed, so it shows well from the first viewing. Sorting comes first, and we plan both around your estate agent&rsquo;s timetable.
- q: Do you sell my home or act as an estate agent?
  a: No. We are not an estate agency. We work alongside your estate agent and your solicitor, but we do not sell, value or market homes, and we do not give legal or financial advice.
- q: Can you help if I am selling to move somewhere smaller?
  a: Yes. This is a common reason to use us. See our <a href="/downsizing-help-for-elderly/">downsizing help</a>, which covers deciding what fits in the smaller home and moving it.
- q: What if my sale and my purchase dates do not line up?
  a: Dates often shift. Gold Prestige includes up to six weeks of storage to bridge the gap between completion and move-in, and storage can be discussed for other packages. See <a href="/storage-during-your-move/">storage between house moves</a>.
- q: Can my family help from a distance?
  a: Yes. Moves are often arranged by adult children on a parent&rsquo;s behalf, by phone or video, with your coordinator keeping everyone updated.
- q: Is the removal insured?
  a: Yes. Every Chayce removal is fully insured against loss or damage in transit, and the cover is set out in your service agreement before the move begins.
- q: Do you work outside Northampton?
  a: Yes. We are based in Northampton and arrange moves across the whole UK.
